SUMMARY:Camino de Brevard w/ WNC Pilgrims
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of the associat
 ion of American Pilgrims on the Camino. The route has been announced on th
 e WNC Camino Group [Facebook Group Page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/A
 VLCamino/announcements).\n\n**Distance:** 4\, 8\, or 11 miles\n**Elevation
  Gain:** 600 ft in small chunks\n**Surface:** Road\n**Pace: 3.2 mph**\n**D
 ogs:** Well-behaved dogs on leash.\n**Gear:** Water\, sunscreen\, snacks\,
  cash / payment method for the farmer's market.\n\n**Origin of Route:** Th
 is route was created by Kacey R for the WNC Chapter of the American Societ
 y of Pilgrims on the Camino.\n\n**All Trails Route Map:** [Brevard Camino 
 Route](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/brevard-camino-k-ra
 tterjee-568e974?u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\nThe route has 3 sections\, each about 4 mi
 les long. Choose the distance that works for you!\n\n**Start:** Transylvan
 ia County Public Library\n212 S Gaston St\, Brevard\, NC 28712\nNote: The 
 library will be closed at the start\, so no bathrooms will be available.\n
 \n**Want to sleep in?** Meet us at the farmer's market next to St. Phillip
 s Church at around 10:30. [256 E Main St\, Brevard\, NC 28712](https://map
 s.app.goo.gl/TeVDqeSEEQD9ieTz7)\n\n**Coffee Break:** There will be a stop 
 at the Farmer's Market at about 10:30. There are bathrooms available at th
 is stop.\n\n**Second Break:** Brevard College\, bathrooms available. Bring
  a lunch.\n\n**Finish:** Around 2 PM.\n\nThis event is hosted / cross-post
 ed with the Society of American Pilgrims on the Camino\, WNC/Asheville Cha
 pter. The American Pilgrims provide education and training for people who 
 want to walk the Camino de Santiago in Spain.\nIf you are unfamiliar with 
 the Camino\, here are a few links to learn more:\n[American Pilgrims on th
 e Camino](https://americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory/western-north-caro
 lina/)\n[Stingy Nomads Camino](https://stingynomads.com/camino-de-santiago
 -walking-guide/)\n**Monthly Bulletin - WNC Chapter - May 2026** [https://s
 hare.google/ljn28ijZqzfzw3qnE](https://share.google/ljn28ijZqzfzw3qnE)\n\n
 **Scenic Asheville Series:** This hike counts as a Wildcard substitute on 
 my Scenic Asheville Series. There are 9 [hikes](https://docs.google.com/do
 cument/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=drivesdk) i
 n the series\; hike them all and receive an [attractive badge](https://doc
 s.google.com/drawings/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit)
  for your backpack. Check your status [HERE](https://docs.google.com/sprea
 dsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).\
 n\n**Guests:** For this hike\, there are no guest restrictions. Bring them
  with you.\n\n**Photo: Brevard Music Center\, Whittington Pfohl Auditorium
 . We will walk to BMC on the last 1/3rd of the hike. If we are lucky\, we 
 may hear a bit of a rehearsal.**\n\n**Disclaimer and Release of Liability:
 **\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that may have traffic an
 d/or hiking on natural surfaces. Participants are responsible for their sa
 fety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and 
 not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organiz
 e this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge t
 hat you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, ill
 nesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with t
 his event. You are responsible for any guests\, dogs or other companions y
 ou bring with you. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Mee
 tup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
